# 🤖 Machine Learning – SMIT Data Science & AI Course

Welcome to the **Machine Learning** module of the **Saylani Mass IT Training (SMIT) Data Science & Artificial Intelligence** program! 

This directory contains Jupyter notebooks, practical assignments, data processing workflows, and hands-on projects covering foundational to advanced machine learning algorithms, evaluation metrics, and feature engineering techniques.

---

## 📂 Module Topics & Structure

| Topic / Folder | Description | Key Libraries & Tools |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **01. Exploratory Data Analysis & Preprocessing** | Data cleaning, feature scaling (Standardization/Normalization), encoding categorical variables, handling missing values, and outlier detection | `Pandas`, `NumPy`, `Seaborn` |
| **02. Supervised Learning – Regression** | Linear Regression, Polynomial Regression, Ridge & Lasso Regularization, and evaluation metrics (MAE, MSE, RMSE, R²) | `scikit-learn`, `Statsmodels` |
| **03. Supervised Learning – Classification** | Logistic Regression, Decision Trees, Random Forests, Support Vector Machines (SVM), K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), and Naive Bayes | `scikit-learn` |
| **04. Model Evaluation & Optimization** | Confusion Matrix, Precision, Recall, F1-Score, ROC-AUC curves, Cross-Validation, and Hyperparameter Tuning (GridSearchCV / RandomizedSearchCV) | `scikit-learn` |
| **05. Ensemble Methods & Boosting** | Bagging, Boosting (AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost), and Stacking classifiers | `xgboost`, `scikit-learn` |
| **06. Unsupervised Learning** | Clustering (K-Means, Hierarchical, DBSCAN) and Dimensionality Reduction (PCA, t-SNE) | `scikit-learn`, `Matplotlib` |
| **07. Model Persistence & Deployment** | Saving models using `pickle` / `joblib` and exposing REST APIs using Flask/Streamlit | `joblib`, `Streamlit` |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

Follow these instructions to set up the environment on your local machine and run the notebooks.

### 1. Prerequisites
Make sure you have installed:
* **Python** (3.8+)
* **Jupyter Notebook** or **VS Code** with Python extensions
* **Git**

### 2. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/buraydkhan/SMIT-DS-AI.git](https://github.com/buraydkhan/SMIT-DS-AI.git)
cd SMIT-DS-AI/"Machine Learning"
